From 4e89f951d714630099ebf0a99dbd91d3ca36fff0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AERA | Erez Yaary <yaary@me.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 05:53:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pdf: pdfgate, PDFs converted for EConvert and EPDF (EPDF's
 protocol)

Erez, 7 Nov 2026: EConvert and EPDF convert either on the Atari or on
the Pi. pdfgate (gateway/pdfgate.py, standard Python 3) takes POST
/convert with EConvert's settings, answers 102 Processing with
X-Progress while aerapdf works, and sends back the converted PDF: the
same bytes EConvert writes on a Falcon (test_pdfgate's real case,
EDOS_01.PDF, byte for byte). aerapdf is EPDF's tools/econvert.c and
src/conv/ built on the Pi with cc and make only (pdf/Makefile), from
EPDF's source copied into pdf/epdf by tools/sync-pdf.sh at a named EPDF
commit, never edited here. One conversion at a time, 600 s and 768 MB at
most, 64 MB of PDF; the log names the Atari and the bytes, never the
file. GET /version answers which EPDF commit it is.

aera-gateway: the pdf service (Pdf: port 8380, --allow, -v; aerapdf
built in prepare(), kept when built from the same pdf/, its fonts and
SOURCE in /opt/aera-gateway-pdf, removed with it); install all includes
it (Erez, 7 Nov), and skips it only in an app's copy of gateway/, which
has no pdf/. Port 8380 and gcc and make on the Pi: Erez's OK, 7 Nov.
Tests: test_pdfgate (13: options, refusals, limits, progress, nothing
left on disk, the real aerapdf against its Direct output), test_installer
(test_pdf, test_pdf_not_built). The protocol: EPDF's docs/PI-GATEWAY.md.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SZeNoDLt48EM4msuao4J1n
